    "project": "research/miller_recursion_audit_20261115/lean",
    "theorem": "MillerRecursionAudit.miller_recursion_certificate",
    "statement": "theorem miller_recursion_certificate : (∀ (K : Type) [Field K] [DecidableEq K] (W : WeierstrassCurve.Affine K) (P : W.Point) (n : ℕ), millerFunction W P n ≠ 0 ∧ principalPointDivisor W (millerFunction W P n) ((miller_has_point_divisor W P n).support_finite W) = millerDivisor W P n ∧ functionValuation W (parameter W ^ (-pointOrder W (millerFunction W P n) 0) * millerFunction W P n - 1) < 1 ∧ (n • P = 0 → principalPointDivisor W (millerFunction W P n) ((miller_has_point_divisor W P n).support_finite W) = (n : ℤ) • Finsupp.single P 1 - (n : ℤ) • Finsupp.single 0 1)) ∧ (∀ (K : Type) [Field K] [DecidableEq K] (W : WeierstrassCurve.Affine K) (P : W.Point) (i j : ℕ) (f g : W.FunctionField), IsMillerFunction W P i f → IsMillerFunction W P j g → IsMillerFunction W P (i + j) (f * g * stepFunction W (i • P) (j • P))) ∧ (∀ (K : Type) [Field K] [DecidableEq K] (W : WeierstrassCurve.Affine K) (P : W.Point), millerFunction W P 1 = 1) ∧ controlCurve.Δ ≠ 0 ∧ twoPoint ≠ 0 ∧ twoPoint + twoPoint = 0 ∧ pointOrder controlCurve (stepFunction controlCurve twoPoint twoPoint) 0 = (-2 : ℤ) ∧ ¬ HasPointDivisor controlCurve (MillerNormValuationAudit.lineFunction controlCurve 4 0 (controlCurve.slope 4 4 0 0)) (chordDivisor controlCurve twoPoint twoPoint)",
    "decl_sha256": "3be8f68d63b18ecd7bf18c28c045b53530c90948403c38146513bc3bcdb1d3bd",
    "scope": "Actual all-n Miller rational functions and normalized principal point divisors for every field/general Weierstrass model/actual nonsingular point. Construct explicit actual addition-step function:1 if either point is O, actual vertical function if points negative, actual chord divided by actual vertical through sum otherwise. Derive nonzero/exact actual local-valuation divisor(P)+(Q)-(P+Q)-(O) in every branch. Recursively construct f0=1,f(n+1)=fn*g(nP,P), prove every fn nonzero with actual finite-support Finsupp principal point divisor n(P)-([n]P)-(n-1)(O), using integer n-1 convention; derive actual n-torsion divisor n(P)-n(O). Actual local orders are official derived normalized adic valuations, with infinity chart valuation already identified. Prove source leading-residue-one normalization using actual parameter X/Y, valuation near-one multiplication/division and actual scaled functions. Prove any valid normalized i,j functions produce a valid normalized i+j function with actual addition step; prove chosen f1=1. Do not infer equality of differently constructed functions from same divisor without uniqueness proof; no binary algorithm runtime/complexity refinement claimed. Actual F5 y²=x³+1 nonzero two-torsion(4,0) control: correct vertical step pole2, treating it as ordinary chord gives pole3 and false actual divisor. Qualified source Def26.3.4/Ex26.3.5/Algorithm29 exceptions survive; no source-refutation/novelty claim. Thirty-three modules include27exact credited earlier modules and6new. Over arbitraryK point divisors on nonsingularKpoints; for elliptic model over algebraically closedK all geometricpoints. SeparateMathlibScheme.localRing/Divisor APIinterop, general all-function divisor finiteness, translation/Weil reciprocity/isogeny/Lang/Cartier/Jacobian/canonicalpairing/MOV-FR/full14 remainopen. Samehost/prover/Mathlib; source header audit procedural only, not independent compiler/parser/physicalhost assurance or signedstanding/canonicalpromotion.",
